>> title: Crème Brûlée
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: custard, cream, vanilla, oven, make-ahead
>> servings: 6
>> time: 5 hr
>> step.5: bake at 325°F in a water bath 40 min
>> step.6: chill 4 hr, then torch the sugar

Preheat the #oven{} to 325°F (165°C) and set six #6-oz ramekins{} in a roasting pan.

Warm @heavy cream{2%cup}(480 mL), @whole milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @vanilla bean{1%whole}(split, seeds scraped in), @table salt{1/8%tsp} in a #saucepan{} until steaming.

Whisk @egg yolks{6%large}(110 g), @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g) to a pale ribbon.

Temper @&(~1)yolks{} with @&(~2)hot cream{}.

Strain @&(~1)custard{} into the ramekins, pour hot water halfway up their sides, and bake at 325°F for ~{40%min}.

Chill @&(~1)custards{} for ~{4%hr}, then sprinkle @turbinado sugar{6%tsp}(24 g) over the tops and torch to a glass crust.
